invariant: INV-28
file: src/srv.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_srv_tcp_init takes a configuration that sets cfg.send, which no
  call of the transport calls, so a server whose caller set one believes
  its records leave through it. tcp_nonblocking.h refuses it at
  configuration time (docs/decisions.md 248).

--- old
    return cfg->buf != NULL && cfg->send == NULL && cfg->recv == NULL &&
           cfg->buf_len >= CH_MIN_RXBUF && cfg->srv.on_record_out != NULL;
--- new
    return cfg->buf != NULL && cfg->recv == NULL && cfg->buf_len >= CH_MIN_RXBUF &&
           cfg->srv.on_record_out != NULL;
